{"seed":{"mim":"225060","entry_type":"phenotype","prefix":"#","title":"CLEFT LIP/PALATE-ECTODERMAL DYSPLASIA SYNDROME","alt_titles":["OROFACIAL CLEFT 7, INCLUDED; OFC7, INCLUDED"],"symbol":"CLPED1","gene_symbols":[],"seed_pmids":[],"max_year":2015},"nodes":[{"id":"entry","type":"Entry","label":"CLEFT LIP/PALATE-ECTODERMAL DYSPLASIA SYNDROME","mim":"225060","entry_type":"phenotype"},{"id":"section:description","type":"Section","label":"description"},{"id":"section:nomenclature","type":"Section","label":"nomenclature"},{"id":"section:cloning_expression","type":"Section","label":"cloning_expression"},{"id":"section:gene_structure","type":"Section","label":"gene_structure"},{"id":"section:clinical_features","type":"Section","label":"clinical_features"},{"id":"section:other_features","type":"Section","label":"other_features"},{"id":"section:biochemical_features","type":"Section","label":"biochemical_features"},{"id":"section:inheritance","type":"Section","label":"inheritance"},{"id":"section:cytogenetics","type":"Section","label":"cytogenetics"},{"id":"section:mapping","type":"Section","label":"mapping"},{"id":"section:heterogeneity","type":"Section","label":"heterogeneity"},{"id":"section:gene_function","type":"Section","label":"gene_function"},{"id":"section:molecular_genetics","type":"Section","label":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"section:genotype_phenotype_correlations","type":"Section","label":"genotype_phenotype_correlations"},{"id":"section:pathogenesis","type":"Section","label":"pathogenesis"},{"id":"section:diagnosis","type":"Section","label":"diagnosis"},{"id":"section:clinical_management","type":"Section","label":"clinical_management"},{"id":"section:population_genetics","type":"Section","label":"population_genetics"},{"id":"section:evolution","type":"Section","label":"evolution"},{"id":"section:animal_model","type":"Section","label":"animal_model"},{"id":"section:history","type":"Section","label":"history"},{"id":"paper:25913853","type":"Paper","label":"Yoshida et al. (2015)","pmid":"25913853","year":2015,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Novel homozygous mutation, c.400C>T (p.Arg134*), in the PVRL1 gene underlies cleft lip/palate-ectodermal dysplasia syndrome in an Asian patient."},{"id":"paper:14494246","type":"Paper","label":"ROSSELLI and GULIENETTI (1961)","pmid":"14494246","year":1961,"content_level":"title","relevance":"background","title":"Ectodermal dysplasia."},{"id":"paper:11559849","type":"Paper","label":"Sözen et al. (2001)","pmid":"11559849","year":2001,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Mutation of PVRL1 is associated with sporadic, non-syndromic cleft lip/palate in northern Venezuela."},{"id":"paper:10932188","type":"Paper","label":"Suzuki et al. (2000)","pmid":"10932188","year":2000,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Mutations of PVRL1, encoding a cell-cell adhesion molecule/herpesvirus receptor, in cleft lip/palate-ectodermal dysplasia."},{"id":"paper:9758630","type":"Paper","label":"Suzuki et al. (1998)","pmid":"9758630","year":1998,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Linkage disequilibrium mapping of the gene for Margarita Island ectodermal dysplasia (ED4) to 11q23."},{"id":"paper:7891379","type":"Paper","label":"Zlotogora (1994)","pmid":"7891379","year":1994,"content_level":"title","relevance":"supporting","title":"Syndactyly, ectodermal dysplasia, and cleft lip/palate."},{"id":"paper:3035184","type":"Paper","label":"Zlotogora et al. (1987)","pmid":"3035184","year":1987,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Cleft lip and palate, pili torti, malformed ears, partial syndactyly of fingers and toes, and mental retardation: a new syndrome?"},{"id":"paper:2845087","type":"Paper","label":"Zlotogora and Ogur (1988)","pmid":"2845087","year":1988,"content_level":"title","relevance":"supporting","title":"Syndactyly, ectodermal dysplasia, and cleft lip and palate."},{"id":"paper:2832607","type":"Paper","label":"Oğur and Yüksel (1988)","pmid":"2832607","year":1988,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Association of syndactyly, ectodermal dysplasia, and cleft lip and palate: report of two sibs from Turkey."},{"id":"paper:2167611","type":"Paper","label":"Rodini and Richieri-Costa (1990)","pmid":"2167611","year":1990,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Autosomal recessive ectodermal dysplasia, cleft lip/palate, mental retardation, and syndactyly: the Zlotogora-Ogur syndrome."},{"id":"paper:1776626","type":"Paper","label":"Bustos et al. (1991)","pmid":"1776626","year":1991,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Autosomal recessive ectodermal dysplasia: I. An undescribed dysplasia/malformation syndrome."},{"id":"finding:3035184:1","type":"Finding","label":"Zlotogora et al. (1987) reported 2 sibs with a syndrome of cleft lip and palate, sparse scalp hair, malformed protruding ears, and partial syndactyly of the fingers and toes. The older child also had mental retardation and pili torti.","pmid":"3035184","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000202","type":"Phenotype","label":"Orofacial cleft","hpo_id":"HP:0000202"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0002209","type":"Phenotype","label":"Sparse scalp hair","hpo_id":"HP:0002209"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000411","type":"Phenotype","label":"Protruding ear","hpo_id":"HP:0000411"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0006101","type":"Phenotype","label":"Finger syndactyly","hpo_id":"HP:0006101"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001770","type":"Phenotype","label":"Toe syndactyly","hpo_id":"HP:0001770"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001249","type":"Phenotype","label":"Intellectual disability","hpo_id":"HP:0001249"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0003777","type":"Phenotype","label":"Pili torti","hpo_id":"HP:0003777"},{"id":"finding:3035184:2","type":"Finding","label":"Zlotogora et al. (1987) concluded that the syndrome in 2 affected sibs was most probably inherited as an autosomal recessive disorder.","pmid":"3035184","section":"inheritance"},{"id":"inh:AR","type":"Inheritance","label":"Autosomal recessive","hpo_id":"HP:0000007"},{"id":"finding:2832607:1","type":"Finding","label":"Oğur and Yüksel (1988) reported 2 Turkish brothers, born to parents who were second cousins, with tetramelic syndactyly, ectodermal dysplasia, cleft lip and palate, renal anomalies, and mental retardation.","pmid":"2832607","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001159","type":"Phenotype","label":"Syndactyly","hpo_id":"HP:0001159"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000951","type":"Phenotype","label":"Abnormality of the skin","hpo_id":"HP:0000951"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000204","type":"Phenotype","label":"Cleft upper lip","hpo_id":"HP:0000204"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000175","type":"Phenotype","label":"Cleft palate","hpo_id":"HP:0000175"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000077","type":"Phenotype","label":"Abnormality of the kidney","hpo_id":"HP:0000077"},{"id":"finding:2832607:2","type":"Finding","label":"Oğur and Yüksel (1988) reported 2 affected brothers born to second-cousin parents. They compared these sibs with previously reported cases and discussed the mode of transmission.","pmid":"2832607","section":"inheritance"},{"id":"finding:2845087:1","type":"Finding","label":"Zlotogora and Ogur (1988) reported syndactyly together with ectodermal dysplasia and cleft lip and palate.","pmid":"2845087","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0410030","type":"Phenotype","label":"Cleft lip","hpo_id":"HP:0410030"},{"id":"finding:2167611:1","type":"Finding","label":"Rodini and Richieri-Costa (1990) reported 3 Brazilian brothers, born to normal consanguineous parents (F = 1/16), who had ectodermal dysplasia, cleft lip/palate, mental retardation, syndactyly of fingers 2-3, accessory nipples, and ear anomalies. The authors discussed the similarities of these brothers to previously reported cases of Zlotogora-Ogur syndrome.","pmid":"2167611","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000968","type":"Phenotype","label":"Ectodermal dysplasia","hpo_id":"HP:0000968"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001233","type":"Phenotype","label":"2-3 finger cutaneous syndactyly","hpo_id":"HP:0001233"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0002558","type":"Phenotype","label":"Supernumerary nipple","hpo_id":"HP:0002558"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000598","type":"Phenotype","label":"Abnormality of the ear","hpo_id":"HP:0000598"},{"id":"finding:2167611:2","type":"Finding","label":"The occurrence of the disorder in 3 brothers born to normal consanguineous parents (F = 1/16) was considered by Rodini and Richieri-Costa (1990) in discussing an autosomal recessive pattern of inheritance for Zlotogora-Ogur syndrome.","pmid":"2167611","section":"inheritance"},{"id":"finding:1776626:1","type":"Finding","label":"Bustos et al. (1991) described 27 individuals from 7 families who were probably related to each other. All had ectodermal dysplasia along with other anomalies. Females were affected as severely as males, and expressivity varied. The families came from a relatively isolated, inbred population on Margarita Island (Nueva Esparta State) in northeastern Venezuela. The authors concluded that the clinical picture did not fit any known ectodermal dysplasia.","pmid":"1776626","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0003828","type":"Phenotype","label":"Variable expressivity","hpo_id":"HP:0003828"},{"id":"finding:1776626:2","type":"Finding","label":"Bustos et al. (1991) found that all parents of affected individuals were normal and that both sexes were equally affected in an inbred population. They concluded that the condition was a newly recognized autosomal recessive dysplasia/malformation syndrome.","pmid":"1776626","section":"inheritance"},{"id":"finding:7891379:1","type":"Finding","label":"Zlotogora (1994) reported on the association of syndactyly, ectodermal dysplasia, and cleft lip/palate.","pmid":"7891379","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001574","type":"Phenotype","label":"Abnormality of the integument","hpo_id":"HP:0001574"},{"id":"finding:9758630:1","type":"Finding","label":"Suzuki et al. (1998) described Margarita Island ectodermal dysplasia (ED4) as an autosomal recessive disorder. Its features are unusual facies, dental anomalies, hypotrichosis, palmoplantar hyperkeratosis, onychodysplasia, syndactyly, and cleft lip/cleft palate.","pmid":"9758630","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001999","type":"Phenotype","label":"Abnormal facial shape","hpo_id":"HP:0001999"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000164","type":"Phenotype","label":"Abnormality of the dentition","hpo_id":"HP:0000164"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0008070","type":"Phenotype","label":"Sparse hair","hpo_id":"HP:0008070"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000972","type":"Phenotype","label":"Palmoplantar hyperkeratosis","hpo_id":"HP:0000972"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0002164","type":"Phenotype","label":"Nail dysplasia","hpo_id":"HP:0002164"},{"id":"finding:9758630:2","type":"Finding","label":"Suzuki et al. (1998) used an affected-only DNA-pooling strategy for linkage disequilibrium mapping and placed the ED4 gene at 11q23. Haplotype analysis of 4 complex Margarita Island ED4 families narrowed the gene to an interval of about 1 to 2 Mb, spanned by just 2 YACs.","pmid":"9758630","section":"mapping"},{"id":"finding:10932188:1","type":"Finding","label":"By positional cloning, Suzuki et al. (2000) identified PVRL1, which encodes nectin-1, an immunoglobulin-related transmembrane cell-cell adhesion molecule of the NAP cell adhesion system, as the gene responsible for autosomal recessive cleft lip/palate-ectodermal dysplasia syndrome (CLPED1; previously ED4).","pmid":"10932188","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"gene:NECTIN1","type":"Gene","label":"NECTIN1"},{"id":"finding:10932188:2","type":"Finding","label":"Suzuki et al. (2000) noted a high frequency of CLPED1 on Margarita Island in the Caribbean Sea and suggested that it might result from resistance of heterozygotes to infection by alpha-herpesviruses, since nectin-1 is the principal cell surface receptor for these viruses (HveC).","pmid":"10932188","section":"population_genetics"},{"id":"finding:10932188:3","type":"Finding","label":"Suzuki et al. (2000) designated the autosomal recessive cleft lip/palate-ectodermal dysplasia syndrome CLPED1, previously known as ED4.","pmid":"10932188","section":"nomenclature"},{"id":"finding:11559849:1","type":"Finding","label":"Sözen et al. (2001) found a highly significant association between heterozygosity for the PVRL1 nonsense mutation W185X and sporadic, non-syndromic cleft lip with or without cleft palate (CL/P) in northern Venezuela. Homozygosity for the same mutation causes the autosomal recessive CL/P syndrome CLPED1 on Margarita Island.","pmid":"11559849","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"variant:NECTIN1:p.W185*","type":"Variant","label":"NECTIN1 p.W185*","gene":"NECTIN1","keys":["p.W185*"],"omim_name":"NECTIN1, TRP185TER"},{"id":"finding:25913853:1","type":"Finding","label":"Yoshida et al. (2015) reported a 7-year-old Japanese boy with cleft lip/palate-ectodermal dysplasia syndrome. He was the first child of a consanguineous marriage. He had hypohidrotic ectodermal dysplasia with sparse, brittle, fine, dry hair and hypodontia, along with a distinctive facial appearance with cleft lip/palate, cutaneous syndactyly of the fingers, and mild mental retardation. Scanning electron microscopy of the hair showed pili torti and pili trianguli et canaliculi.","pmid":"25913853","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000966","type":"Phenotype","label":"Hypohidrosis","hpo_id":"HP:0000966"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0004779","type":"Phenotype","label":"Brittle scalp hair","hpo_id":"HP:0004779"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0011359","type":"Phenotype","label":"Dry hair","hpo_id":"HP:0011359"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000668","type":"Phenotype","label":"Hypodontia","hpo_id":"HP:0000668"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001256","type":"Phenotype","label":"Mild intellectual disability","hpo_id":"HP:0001256"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0002235","type":"Phenotype","label":"Pili canaliculi","hpo_id":"HP:0002235"},{"id":"finding:25913853:2","type":"Finding","label":"Yoshida et al. (2015) analyzed exon 2 of the PVRL1 gene in the Japanese boy with cleft lip/palate-ectodermal dysplasia syndrome and found a novel homozygous nonsense mutation, c.400C>T (p.Arg134*). Both of his consanguineous parents were heterozygous for the mutation. The authors noted that all 4 PVRL1 mutations reported in this syndrome so far, including this one, produce truncated proteins that lack the transmembrane and intracellular domains of nectin-1. These domains are needed to start the cell-cell adhesion process.","pmid":"25913853","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"variant:NECTIN1:c.400C>T","type":"Variant","label":"NECTIN1 c.400C>T / p.R134*","gene":"NECTIN1","keys":["c.400C>T","p.R134*"],"omim_name":"NECTIN1, ARG134TER"}],"edges":[{"src":"paper:3035184","rel":"reports","dst":"finding:3035184:1"},{"src":"finding:3035184:1","rel":"in_section","dst":"section:clinical_features"},{"src":"finding:3035184:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0000202","pmid":"3035184","present":true,"frequency":"2/2","text":"cleft lip and palate"},{"src":"finding:3035184:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0002209","pmid":"3035184","present":true,"frequency":"2/2","text":"sparse scalp hair"},{"src":"finding:3035184:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0000411","pmid":"3035184","present":true,"frequency":"2/2","text":"malformed protruding ears"},{"src":"finding:3035184:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0006101","pmid":"3035184","present":true,"frequency":"2/2","text":"partial syndactyly of fingers"},{"src":"finding:3035184:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0001770","pmid":"3035184","present":true,"frequency":"2/2","text":"partial syndactyly of toes"},{"src":"finding:3035184:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0001249","pmid":"3035184","present":true,"frequency":"1/2","text":"mental retardation"},{"src":"finding:3035184:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0003777","pmid":"3035184","present":true,"frequency":"1/2","text":"pili torti"},{"src":"paper:3035184","rel":"reports","dst":"finding:303